// spec: ERR-006
//
// A type error carries the same three-line excerpt a parse error does, and
// names both types.
//
// ⚠️ This case was defects/DEF-29 until the checker was fixed.  It said
// 'Type mismatch!' and nothing else -- no file, no line, no token, neither
// type, and the same five words for every mismatch the checker could find.
// The information was discarded rather than absent: every one of the five
// sites that raises had the token in hand.
//
// ⚠️ The caret names the DECLARATION, not the offending value.  A literal
// carries no token [Expr.a24], so there is nothing to point at inside the
// initializer without giving one to every expression.

var Count : Integer := 'text';
